we cannot leave her alone in poland ina  baranov was desperate to get her mother  home having already endured the  terrifying early days of the russian  invasion alone in odessa she was  stranded in poland waiting for a  canadian visa no no i thought it's gonna  be fast because my mom  she is first 85 years old second she has  place to go she got depressed you know  because she said how long how long the  baranovs did not have an answer after  several weeks waiting with her mother  baranov's husband ran out of vacation  time so she had to fly to warsaw to take  his place  alexandra aslanova and her two young  daughters were facing a similar  frustration in germany her sister's home  in winnipeg had beds and toys to welcome  them but after submitting three visa  applications only one had come through  it's so cruel when when you give a visa  to one family member but not another the  worst thing is that there's nobody to  to talk to you have to deal with  some  website run by  a company which is not even the part of  the government what i saw there was  really  shocking and embarrassing and i felt  like somewhere between nausea and like i  wanted to cry alexander polowski found  this scene at canada's visa processing  office in berlin  after trying to help a ukrainian woman  navigate the system he was surprised to  find the place inaccessible to those who  had traveled there some of them had been  telling me that they are sleeping in  their car like not in the street like in  sleeping bikes but in their cars  directly in front of this office and  that one one lady and multiple people  actually told me that they were had been  staying there for three days polowsky  says the ukrainian woman he helped left  the office empty-handed that day only  able to get an appointment online a  month later in paris ina baranov's  mother was finally able to get her visa  after a lawyer became involved alexandra  aslanova's daughters eventually received  their visas too after several weeks of  unexplained delays  finally allowing these families to begin  new chapters now that their limbo is  over at last heather urex west global  news
 

